# Scoped, dated exceptions for the image-scan gate.
#
# This file is read by the GATE step of .github/workflows/trivy-scan.yml only,
# via that step's trivyignores input. The report step that feeds the GitHub
# Security tab does NOT read it, so every advisory listed here stays fully
# visible in the Security tab and in the SARIF record. Suppressing a finding here
# removes it from what blocks a build; it does not remove it from what is on the
# record.
#
# The name matters. Trivy reads a file called .trivyignore from the working
# directory automatically, which would apply it to the report step as well and
# destroy the property above. Do not rename this file to .trivyignore or
# .trivyignore.yaml.
#
# Never widen the gate's severity threshold to get a build through. Add a named,
# dated entry here with an exit condition instead, and remove it when the exit
# condition is met.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Added 2026-09-17 — starlette, still on 0.x by choice
# Updated 2026-09-18 — the blocker described here no longer exists
#
# Installed starlette is 0.49.1. The fixes are in starlette 1.1.0 and 1.3.1.
#
# This entry originally said those fixes could not be installed, because fastapi
# 0.121.0 constrained starlette <0.50.0. That is no longer true. fastapi 0.141.1
# requires only starlette>=0.46.0, and the 401-vs-403 change that came with the
# fastapi releases in between has been decided: FastAPI's HTTPBearer now answers
# a missing Authorization header with 401 rather than 403, which is the correct
# code, and the one test that asserted 403 for that case has been updated. The
# frontend's axios interceptor redirects on 401, so the no-token case now
# redirects to /login where it previously surfaced a raw error.
#
# What remains is only that backend/requirements.txt still pins starlette 0.49.1.
# Measured 2026-09-18 on an image built from main: starlette 0.49.1 leaves 2 HIGH
# at the gate (the two below); starlette 1.6.0 takes the gate to 0 CRITICAL and
# 0 HIGH with the backend suite at 203 passing, unchanged from baseline.
#
# EXIT CONDITION: when backend/requirements.txt moves to starlette >= 1.3.1,
# delete this whole file AND remove the trivyignores line from the Gate step in
# .github/workflows/trivy-scan.yml, in the same commit. Both halves are
# required: trivy-action's entrypoint hard-errors ("cannot find ignorefile") and
# exits 1 when a file named in trivyignores is missing, so deleting this file on
# its own turns every Gate run red. The work that used to block the move is done.
#
# Exposure in the meantime: this deployment model assumes a private network or
# VPN/tunnel, per SECURITY.md, and is not exposed to the public internet.

# starlette: SSRF and NTLM credential theft via UNC paths in StaticFiles.
# Fixed in starlette 1.1.0.
CVE-2026-48818

# starlette: request.form() limits silently ignored for
# application/x-www-form-urlencoded, enabling denial of service.
# Fixed in starlette 1.3.1.
CVE-2026-54283
